  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Great teaching is built on the human connection between a teacher and student. As technology evolves, our goal isn't to replace that connection, but to support it.

At ISTE, we showcased new tools across Google Classroom, Chromebooks and Gemini designed to keep educators at the forefront of AI and providing students with personalized support.

Key updates include:
- Study notebooks in Gemini that create personalized lessons and quizzes that adapt as a student learns.
- A new Classroom app in Gemini that helps educators with everyday tasks using their class context.

Coming soon: 
- Teacher-led AI activities in Google Classroom that are grounded in a school’s curriculum and give insights into student understanding.
- No-cost ACT and GRE practice tests developed in partnership with <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-princeton-review?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>The Princeton Review</a>.
Guided Learning tools for Chromebooks to help students stay focused.

To further our commitment, our Google Educator Series is providing free AI training to every educator in the U.S. in partnership with ISTE+ASCD.

Learn more about all of our education updates from ISTE ➡️ <a class="link" href="https://goo.gle/4xQqdFp?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://goo.gle/4xQqdFp</a></p>
<!---->  </div>



        

        
            
      
    
    
    

