    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">If you read about AI or are using AI tools, you’ve probably heard the phrase “full-stack.” It’s the driving force that lets us deliver powerful, cost-efficient products to developers and everyday users.

But what does "full-stack AI" actually mean? We asked <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/seroter?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Richard Seroter</a>, Chief Evangelist at Google Cloud, to break it all down 👇

